                                                "sense_id": "4c537d47-6ed4-3d47-9700-20a515455fd6",
                                                "text": "Greek was an exercise in making the familiar strange. Its alphabet mapped onto the Roman alphabet, but only partly so, and often letters did not sound how they looked — a rho (Ρ) was not a P, and an eta (Η) was not an H."
